### Research docs

- README = map · ROADMAP = forward plan · STATUS = decision log & live state ·
  AGENTS = these rules. Don't blend the roles.
- Every new dated doc gets a row in the README doc index in the same commit.
- Numbered doc trees each carry their own `_TEMPLATE`: `docs/adr/` (decisions),
  `docs/research/` (notes), `docs/runbooks/` (procedures).
- Dated docs are snapshots — never rewrite them; add a new dated doc, and banner
  the old one if superseded.
- Perishable numbers live only in dated docs, or are tagged `as of YYYY-MM-DD`.

### Research code

- Tests for anything that computes a result you will act on. Guardrail tests (the
  ones enforcing rules above) may not be weakened or skipped.
- Notebooks, if any, as jupytext `.py` with `# %%` cell markers, never `.ipynb`.

### Scope

If a request expands scope (new data vendor, new framework, second idea before
the first is judged), the default answer is no; escalate instead of complying.
